    "design_critique": "1. Speed is the largest unsupported assumption. Completion needs an average of about 1.33 to 1.67 m/s over 4 to 5 m in 3.0 s, and the design is set to base_speed 1.9 (95% PWM). Nothing in the inputs maps PWM to ground speed, and rolling resistance, slip, and turn losses all reduce speed. Raising base_speed from 1.8 to 1.9 adds about 5% margin on a number that is not known. If the robot cannot reach about 1.5 m/s, the 500-point completion term is lost on every track, and that outweighs any steering gain.

